    <MultiLanguageText Lang="de-DE" />
    <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-GB" />
    <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">
If the input value (x) is located in the dead band range (-bandBorder &lt; x &lt; +bandBorder), the output value is set to zero.
However, if it is at or below (–bandBorder) the output will be x – bandBorder.
If the input value is at or above +bandBorder, x + bandBorder is set as output value.
The dead band – symmetrical around the zero point – can be set using the bandBorder parameter.

| Input value x                    | Return value   |
| -------------------------------- | -------------- |
| x &lt;= -bandBorder                 | x + bandBorder |
| -bandBorder &lt; x &lt; bandBorder     | 0              |
| x &gt;= bandBorder                  | x - bandBorder |

![Dead band fitler](DeadBand.png)

</MultiLanguageText>
